INT. GREAT HALL OF A SLEEPING KINGDOM - TWILIGHT

A long table laid for a feast no one has touched. Candles burn low. Every guest is awake, nobody eats.

QUEEN RAVENNA, 50s, in a gown the color of old wine, sits at the head. THANE ALDRIC, 60s, broad, scarred, stares into his cup. SEER IMBOLC, 70s, blind, hands folded on her cane. BARD FENWICK, 30s, a lute on his knee, strings muted. DAME DOLORES, 40s, knight-errant, mud on her boots, gloves still on. LARK, 12, the page, stands behind the queen's chair holding a jug.

RAVENNA
Seer. You may speak.

IMBOLC
I'd rather not.

RAVENNA
That wasn't a request.

IMBOLC
Then I'll say it once. The king sleeps tonight and does not wake.

ALDRIC
The king is already asleep.

IMBOLC
Not that sleep.

Fenwick's hand slips on the lute. A string twangs and dies. Dolores reaches slowly for her sword hilt. Lark's jug trembles.

RAVENNA
(very softly)
Who among us?

IMBOLC
The one who pours.

Every head turns. Lark goes white.
